IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sat-dates`
IMPORT `sat-rules`

-- State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) -- the questions of the APPLICANT (and of the individual party).
--
-- SEAT: the individual who brings a matter to the Tribunal -- most often a person asking for review of a government or
-- licensing decision made about them, or a person bringing a claim the enabling Act sends to the Tribunal -- and the
-- individual who is a party to a Tribunal proceeding: "Is this a review?", "Do I get notice and reasons, and by when?",
-- "Does my review stop the decision?", "Who may represent me?", "Can the Tribunal dismiss my case?", "Will I pay costs?",
-- "Can I get more time?", "Is my case a minor proceeding?", "Can I be fined?", "Can I appeal, and by when?". The
-- Tribunal, the executive officer, the President, the decision-maker and the courts get no seat: their judgments,
-- orders and leave are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of sat-rules.l4. The
-- time limits are DEONTIC rules run inside the "Can I still ..." questions and the reasons-order question; no question
-- takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004", State
-- of Western Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004: the applicant's questions`

§§ `Which kind of matter I have`

@export Is my matter in the State Administrative Tribunal's review jurisdiction (a review of a decision made about me) or its original jurisdiction (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 13-15, 17)? It is a review where the Act that sends it to the Tribunal (the enabling Act) expressly or necessarily involves reviewing a decision; a referral of the rejection of your application is a review, and a referral by the executive officer of whether to reject it is original.
GIVEN `how did it come to the Tribunal` IS A `How the matter came` @desc How the matter came before the Tribunal: under an enabling Act (the usual case); a referral, at your request, of the executive officer's rejection of your application or of conditions on it (s 44(3)); or a referral by the executive officer of whether your application could be rejected (s 44(4))
      `does it involve reviewing a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what the enabling Act lets you bring to the Tribunal is (expressly or necessarily) a review of a decision someone made, rather than a claim or application decided for the first time by the Tribunal
GIVETH A `Jurisdiction`
`Is my matter a review or original` MEANS
    `ss 15, 17 -- the jurisdiction` `how did it come to the Tribunal` `does it involve reviewing a decision`

§§ `Review and judicial review`

@export Am I barred from starting a Tribunal review because of judicial review proceedings about the same decision (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 19(3)(a), (c), (5))? You cannot start both at once, nor a Tribunal review after judicial review has started, unless the judicial review was dismissed or struck out for a procedural defect, or because the court thought it inappropriate or the Tribunal more appropriate.
GIVEN `has judicial review been started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether judicial review proceedings (certiorari, mandamus, prohibition, another prerogative writ or a declaration) have been started about the decision, before or at the same time as your Tribunal application
      `was it started at the same time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were started at the same time as the Tribunal review would be
      `was it dismissed for a s 19(5) reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judicial review proceedings were dismissed or struck out for procedural defects and not on their merits, or because the court found them inappropriate or a Tribunal proceeding more appropriate
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I barred from a Tribunal review by judicial review` MEANS
    `s 19(3)(a), (c), (5) -- a Tribunal review is barred` `has judicial review been started` `was it started at the same time` `was it dismissed for a s 19(5) reason`

@export Am I barred from seeking judicial review of the decision because I started a Tribunal review (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 19(3)(b), (4))? Once the Tribunal review has started you cannot later seek judicial review of the original decision, even after the review ends, unless the Tribunal struck it out because judicial review is more appropriate; judicial review of the Tribunal's own decision is not affected.
GIVEN `has my Tribunal review been started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Tribunal proceeding for review of the decision has been started (it starts when the executive officer accepts the application)
      `was it struck out for judicial review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal struck the review out under s 50(1) because it considered judicial review proceedings more appropriate
      `is it about the Tribunal's own decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the judicial review you want is of the Tribunal's own decision rather than the original decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I barred from judicial review by my Tribunal review` MEANS
    `s 19(3)(b), (4) -- judicial review is barred` `has my Tribunal review been started` `was it struck out for judicial review` `is it about the Tribunal's own decision`

§§ `Notice and reasons from the decision-maker`

@export Must the decision-maker give me written notice of a decision I can have reviewed, and of my right to a review (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 20)? Yes, unless the decision does not adversely affect you and is a decision not to impose a liability, penalty or limitation or puts you in the most favourable category of benefit, or the regulations exempt it. A failure does not make the decision invalid.
GIVEN `does it adversely affect me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision adversely affects your interests
      `is it a decision not to impose something` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a decision not to impose a liability, penalty or any kind of limitation on a person
      `does it give me the most favourable category` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is made under an Act with several categories of entitlement to a benefit and puts you in the most favourable one
      `is it exempted by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is of a kind the regulations prescribe for s 20(2)(b)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I be given notice of the decision and my review right` MEANS
    `s 20(1), (2) -- I must be given notice` `does it adversely affect me` `is it a decision not to impose something` `does it give me the most favourable category` `is it exempted by the regulations`

@export By when can I ask the decision-maker for a written statement of reasons for a decision I can have reviewed (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 21(1)-(3))? In writing, within 28 days after the decision, or within 28 days after you were given notice of it under s 20 if that is later. You cannot ask if you already have a statement with the reasons and findings, or if the enabling Act gives you its own right to reasons.
GIVEN `do I already have a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision-maker has already given you a written statement of the reasons and the findings on material facts (in the decision or separately)
      `does the enabling Act give its own right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act has its own provisions under which you have, or could have had, a right to such a statement
      `when was the decision made` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was made
      `must I be notified under s 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 20(1) applies, so that the decision-maker must give you written notice (the answer to the notice question)
      `have I been notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that written notice has been given to you
      `when was I notified` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given (any date if not)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when can I ask for reasons` MEANS
    `s 21(3) -- the time limit to request reasons` (`s 21(1), (2) -- I may request reasons` `do I already have a statement of reasons` `does the enabling Act give its own right`) `when was the decision made` `must I be notified under s 20` `have I been notified` `when was I notified`

@export Can I still ask the decision-maker for a written statement of reasons on this day (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 21(3))? The time limit is run as a duty to request within the 28 days; a request on the last day is in time.
GIVEN `do I already have a statement of reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision-maker has already given you a written statement of the reasons and the findings on material facts
      `does the enabling Act give its own right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act has its own provisions giving you a right to such a statement
      `when was the decision made` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was made
      `must I be notified under s 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 20(1) applies, so that the decision-maker must give you written notice
      `have I been notified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that written notice has been given to you
      `when was I notified` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was given (any date if not)
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or would make) the written request
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still ask for reasons on this day` MEANS
    `the person can take` `request a statement of reasons` `running from` `when was the decision made` `under` (`By when can I ask for reasons` `do I already have a statement of reasons` `does the enabling Act give its own right` `when was the decision made` `must I be notified under s 20` `have I been notified` `when was I notified`) `on` `the day I ask`

@export By when must the decision-maker give me the statement of reasons I asked for (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 21(4))? As soon as practicable, and in any case within 28 days after your request.
GIVEN `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the written request
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I get the statement of reasons` MEANS
    `s 21(4) -- the last day for the statement` `the day I asked`

@export The decision-maker has not given me the statement of reasons I asked for: can I apply to the Tribunal for an order that they give it (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 21(4), 22, 23(2))? Yes once the 28 days after your request have passed without the statement (or a notice that it cannot be given because leaving out protected matter would make it misleading). You must notify the decision-maker of your application within the time in the rules.
GIVEN `could I ask for reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were entitled to ask for a statement of reasons (no earlier statement, and no separate right under the enabling Act)
      `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the written request
      `have they responded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision-maker has given you the statement, or told you under s 23(2) that it is not being given because it would be false or misleading without protected matter
      `the day they responded` IS A DATE @desc The day they did so (any date if not)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or would apply) to the Tribunal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply for an order for reasons` MEANS
    `s 22(1) -- I may apply for an order for reasons` `could I ask for reasons` `the day I asked` `have they responded` `the day they responded` `the day I apply`

§§ `While my review runs`

@export Does starting my Tribunal review stop the decision from operating (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 25)? No, unless the Tribunal orders a stay or the enabling Act says otherwise. You can ask the Tribunal for a stay; it may require an undertaking as to costs or damages.
GIVEN `has the Tribunal ordered a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has made an order staying the operation of the decision under s 25(2)
      `does the enabling Act say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act states otherwise about the effect of a review on the decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the decision stayed by my review` MEANS
    `s 25 -- the decision is stayed by the review` `has the Tribunal ordered a stay` `does the enabling Act say otherwise`

@export Can the decision-maker change or replace the decision after I have started my review (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 26)? Not unless the enabling Act permits it, the parties consent, or the Tribunal invites the decision-maker to reconsider it.
GIVEN `has my review started` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your Tribunal review has started
      `does the enabling Act allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act permits the decision-maker to vary or replace the decision
      `do all parties consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the parties to the review consent
      `has the Tribunal invited reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has invited the decision-maker under s 31 to reconsider the decision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the decision-maker change the decision during my review` MEANS
    `s 26 -- the decision-maker may change the decision` `has my review started` `does the enabling Act allow it` `do all parties consent` `has the Tribunal invited reconsideration`

@export From when does the Tribunal's decision take effect (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 29(5), 82)? A decision on a review that affirms, varies or replaces the original decision has effect from when the original would have had effect, unless the enabling Act or the Tribunal orders otherwise; other decisions take effect immediately, or at a later time stated in them.
GIVEN `is it a review decision affirming, varying or replacing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal's decision affirms, varies, or substitutes its own decision for, the decision under review (not sending it back)
      `does the enabling Act or an order say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act or the Tribunal's order says otherwise about when it has effect
      `does it state a later time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For any other decision: whether the decision states a later time for it to come into effect
GIVETH A `When the decision takes effect`
`When does the Tribunal's decision take effect` MEANS
    `ss 29(5), 82 -- when the decision takes effect` `is it a review decision affirming, varying or replacing` `does the enabling Act or an order say otherwise` `does it state a later time`

§§ `Representation and interpreters`

@export May this person represent me at a hearing of the State Administrative Tribunal (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 39, 93(3))? A lawyer may, unless struck off or suspended; anyone else only if you are a public sector employee represented by an authorised colleague, the person has particular relevant knowledge or experience, the Tribunal agrees, or the regulations or rules allow it. After a no legal representation election in a minor proceeding, no lawyer or legally qualified person may.
GIVEN `is the person a lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is a legal practitioner
      `is the person struck off or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has been struck off the roll of practitioners or is suspended from practice
      `do the regulations or rules exclude the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations or the Tribunal's rules prevent this person, or people of their class, from representing a party
      `was a no legal representation election made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant in a minor proceeding has made a no legal representation election under s 93(2)(a)
      `is the person legally qualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person (if not a WA lawyer) is entitled to practise law elsewhere, or is someone the Tribunal considers has qualifications or experience in law likely to give an advantage
      `is it my public sector colleague` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a party because of your duties as a public sector employee and the person is another public sector employee authorised by you
      `does the person have relevant experience` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person has particular knowledge or experience relevant to the matter (not experience gained as, or representing, a party in another Tribunal proceeding)
      `has the Tribunal agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has agreed to the person representing you, with any conditions it set met
      `do the regulations or rules allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations or the rules authorise the representation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May this person represent me` MEANS
    `s 39, s 93(3) -- the person may represent me` `is the person a lawyer` `is the person struck off or suspended` `do the regulations or rules exclude the person` `was a no legal representation election made` `is the person legally qualified` `is it my public sector colleague` `does the person have relevant experience` `has the Tribunal agreed` `do the regulations or rules allow it`

@export May I have an interpreter or other helper in my Tribunal proceeding (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 41)? Yes, unless the Tribunal directs otherwise.
GIVEN `has the Tribunal said no` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has directed that you may not be assisted by an interpreter or other person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`May I have an interpreter` MEANS
    `s 41 -- I may have an interpreter` `has the Tribunal said no`

§§ `Starting the proceeding`

@export Can we bring our applications to the Tribunal together as one proceeding (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 42(4))? Only if the facts or circumstances of each person's interests are the same or related.
GIVEN `are our facts the same or related` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the facts or circumstances relating to each person's interests are the same or related
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can we apply jointly` MEANS
    `s 42(4) -- we may commence jointly` `are our facts the same or related`

@export My application was rejected, or accepted on conditions: can I have that reviewed by the Tribunal (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 44(3), (5), (6))? Yes: ask the executive officer to refer it to the Tribunal, who must do so. No fee is payable, but there is no appeal from the Tribunal's decision on it.
GIVEN `what happened to my application` IS A `What happened to my application` @desc What the executive officer did with your application: accepted it without conditions, accepted it on conditions, rejected it, or not yet decided
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I have the rejection reviewed` MEANS
    `s 44(3) -- I may have the rejection or conditions reviewed` `what happened to my application`

@export Must I give this person a copy of my application (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 45)? Once it is accepted, yes for each other party, anyone entitled to a copy or notice, and anyone the Tribunal directs, unless the executive officer has given or undertaken to give it, the Tribunal has dispensed with it, or the rules exempt you.
GIVEN `has it been accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the executive officer has accepted your application
      `is the person one I must serve` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person is another party, someone entitled under this Act or the enabling Act to a copy or notice of the application, or someone the Tribunal has directed you to give a copy to
      `has the executive officer done it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the executive officer has given, or undertaken to give, the person a copy
      `has the Tribunal dispensed with it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has ordered that you need not give this person a copy (after unsuccessful attempts, or where no injustice would follow)
      `do the rules exempt me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules exempt you from giving this person a copy
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I give this person a copy of my application` MEANS
    `s 45(1), (2) -- I must give the person a copy` `has it been accepted` `is the person one I must serve` `has the executive officer done it` `has the Tribunal dispensed with it` `do the rules exempt me`

§§ `Dismissal, conferences and mediation (if it has come to this)`

@export What can the Tribunal do if it believes I am conducting my case so as to disadvantage another party, or if I miss a compulsory conference (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 48, 53)? An applicant's case can be dismissed or struck out; another party can have the case decided against them or be struck out. Missing a conference lets it go ahead without you, and with all present agreeing, lets the presiding member decide against you or strike you out.
GIVEN `what did I do` IS A `What I did` @desc What happened: you conducted the proceeding in a way the Tribunal believes unnecessarily disadvantages another party (for example not following orders, deceiving, not attending hearings), or you did not attend a properly convened compulsory conference
      `am I the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the applicant (the person who brought the matter)
      `did all present agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a missed conference: whether a Tribunal member was presiding and all the parties present agreed to the Tribunal acting against the absent party
GIVETH A `What the Tribunal may do`
`What can the Tribunal do about my conduct or absence` MEANS
    `ss 48, 53 -- what the Tribunal may do` `what did I do` `am I the applicant` `did all present agree`

@export My proceeding was dismissed or struck out (withdrawn, want of prosecution, frivolous or abusive, or disadvantaging conduct): can I start it again (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 49)? Not the same kind of proceeding about the same matter without the leave of a judicial member.
GIVEN `was it dismissed under s 46, 47 or 48` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the earlier proceeding was dismissed or struck out under s 46 (withdrawal, want of prosecution), s 47 (frivolous, vexatious, abuse) or s 48 (disadvantaging conduct)
      `is it the same kind and matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the new proceeding is of the same kind and about the same matter
      `has a judicial member given leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President or a Deputy President has given leave to start it again
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I start my dismissed proceeding again` MEANS
    `s 49 -- I may commence again` `was it dismissed under s 46, 47 or 48` `is it the same kind and matter` `has a judicial member given leave`

@export Can what was said or done at a compulsory conference or mediation be used as evidence later in my proceeding (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 55)? No, unless all parties agree, it is evidence of directions or orders made there (or their reasons), or it is relevant to a prosecution for giving false or misleading information, a contempt, or an order made against an absent party.
GIVEN `do all parties agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether all parties agree to the evidence being admitted
      `is it about directions or orders made there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is evidence of directions given or orders made at the conference or mediation, or of the reasons for them
      `is it for a false information, contempt or absent-party matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is relevant to a proceeding for an offence of giving false or misleading information, a contempt proceeding under s 100, or a proceeding about an order made under s 53(b)(i) against an absent party
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can what was said at the conference be used later` MEANS
    `s 55 -- it may be used later` `do all parties agree` `is it about directions or orders made there` `is it for a false information, contempt or absent-party matter`

§§ `Evidence and witnesses`

@export Can I be ordered to pay towards the cost of an expert the Tribunal brought in (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 64)? Only if, before getting the help, the Tribunal told you it intended to, the likely costs and your likely share, and gave you a chance to be heard.
GIVEN `was I told of the plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal told you, before getting the assistance, that it intended to obtain it
      `was I told the likely cost` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it told you the likely costs of the assistance
      `was I told my likely share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it told you the likely amount of your payment or contribution
      `was I given a chance to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it gave you an opportunity to be heard on the matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be made to pay for the Tribunal's expert` MEANS
    `s 64 -- I may be ordered to pay for the expert` `was I told of the plan` `was I told the likely cost` `was I told my likely share` `was I given a chance to be heard`

@export Am I entitled to fees and allowances for attending as a witness (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 66(5))? Yes if you attended under a summons: the amounts in the rules, or if none, as the Tribunal determines; the Tribunal decides which party pays.
GIVEN `did I attend under a summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you attended (or produced documents) in answer to a Tribunal summons
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to witness fees` MEANS
    `s 66(5) -- I am entitled to witness fees` `did I attend under a summons`

@export Can an answer I was required to give the Tribunal be used against me in a criminal case (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 68)? You must answer even if it might incriminate you, but the answer (and the fact you produced a document) cannot be used in criminal proceedings against you, except for perjury or an offence of giving a false or misleading answer.
GIVEN `was I required to answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the answer or produced the document to comply with a requirement under this Act in a Tribunal proceeding
      `is it a perjury or false answer case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the criminal proceedings are for perjury or for an offence under this Act arising from the answer being false or misleading
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my answer be used against me` MEANS
    `s 68(2) -- my answer may be used against me in criminal proceedings` `was I required to answer` `is it a perjury or false answer case`

§§ `The decision and its reasons`

@export Must the Tribunal give its decision in writing (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 74)? Yes if it is a final decision, it was reserved, the rules require it, or a party asks.
GIVEN `is it a final decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision disposes of the matter raised in the application
      `was it reserved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal reserved its decision (did not decide on the spot)
      `do the rules require it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules state that this decision has to be in writing
      `has a party asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you or another party has requested the decision in writing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the decision be in writing` MEANS
    `s 74 -- the decision must be in writing` `is it a final decision` `was it reserved` `do the rules require it` `has a party asked`

@export By when must the Tribunal give a decision it reserved, with its reasons (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 76)? Within 90 days after the day it reserved it, unless the President extends that. A late decision is still valid.
GIVEN `the day it was reserved` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal reserved its decision
      `has the President extended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President has extended the period
      `the extended day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended period (any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the reserved decision be given` MEANS
    `s 76 -- the last day for a reserved decision` `the day it was reserved` `has the President extended it` `the extended day`

@export By when can I ask the Tribunal for its reasons in writing (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 78(1))? If it decided without reserving and did not give written reasons, within 28 days after the day the decision was given.
GIVEN `was it reserved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal reserved its decision (if so, written reasons come with it under s 76)
      `were written reasons given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has already given its reasons in writing (a transcript of oral reasons counts, s 79)
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was given
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when can I ask for the Tribunal's written reasons` MEANS
    `s 78(1) -- the time limit to request written reasons` `was it reserved` `were written reasons given` `the day of the decision`

@export Can I still ask the Tribunal for its reasons in writing on this day (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 78(1))? The 28 days are run as a duty to request in time; a request on the last day is in time.
GIVEN `was it reserved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal reserved its decision
      `were written reasons given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has already given its reasons in writing
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision was given
      `the day I ask` IS A DATE @desc The day you make (or would make) the request
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still ask for the Tribunal's written reasons on this day` MEANS
    `the person can take` `request written reasons from the Tribunal` `running from` `the day of the decision` `under` (`s 78(1) -- the time limit to request written reasons` `was it reserved` `were written reasons given` `the day of the decision`) `on` `the day I ask`

@export By when must the Tribunal give me the written reasons I asked for (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 78(2))? Within 90 days after the day it receives your request, unless the President extends that.
GIVEN `the day it got my request` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal received your request
      `has the President extended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the President has extended the period
      `the extended day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended period (any date if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the Tribunal give written reasons` MEANS
    `s 78(2) -- the last day for written reasons` `the day it got my request` `has the President extended it` `the extended day`

@export The Tribunal decided against me at a hearing I did not attend: can I apply to have that decision reviewed (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 84(2)-(4))? Yes if it was made about you, you did not appear and were not represented at the hearing (a compulsory conference or mediation does not count), and you apply within the time limits in the Tribunal's rules. Not if a no appeals election was made in the proceeding (s 93(5)).
GIVEN `was it made about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made in respect of you
      `was a no appeals election made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant made a no appeals election in this minor proceeding (s 93(2)(c)); the decision is then final and not subject to review (s 93(5))
      `did I appear or was I represented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appeared, or were represented, at the hearing at which (or after which) the decision was made
      `am I within the rules' time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are within the time limit the Tribunal's rules set for this application
      `do the rules need leave for this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already made as many applications about this matter as the rules allow without leave, and have no leave
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I have the decision made in my absence reviewed` MEANS
    `s 84(2)-(4) -- I may apply for review of a decision made in my absence` `was it made about me` `was a no appeals election made` `did I appear or was I represented` `am I within the rules' time` `do the rules need leave for this one`

@export If I apply for review of a decision made in my absence, must the Tribunal review it (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 84(5))? Yes if it is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse for not attending or being represented; it may then revoke or vary the decision.
GIVEN `was it made about me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made in respect of you
      `was a no appeals election made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant made a no appeals election in this minor proceeding (s 93(2)(c)); the decision is then final and not subject to review (s 93(5))
      `did I appear or was I represented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you appeared, or were represented, at the hearing
      `am I within the rules' time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied within the time limit in the Tribunal's rules
      `do the rules need leave for this one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the rules require leave for this further application and you have none
      `is the Tribunal satisfied of my excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal is satisfied you had a reasonable excuse for not attending or being represented
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must the Tribunal review the decision made in my absence` MEANS
    `s 84(5) -- the Tribunal must review it` (`s 84(2)-(4) -- I may apply for review of a decision made in my absence` `was it made about me` `was a no appeals election made` `did I appear or was I represented` `am I within the rules' time` `do the rules need leave for this one` EQUALS JUST TRUE) `is the Tribunal satisfied of my excuse`

@export How do I enforce a Tribunal decision in my favour that the other side has not complied with (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 85, 86)? An order to pay you money: file a certified copy and your affidavit of the amount unpaid in a court that can hear that amount. Any other decision: file a certified copy, your affidavit and a judicial member's certificate in the Supreme Court. No filing fee either way.
GIVEN `is it an order to pay me money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision is a monetary order (an order requiring payment of money, including costs) in your favour
GIVETH A `How to enforce`
`How do I enforce the decision` MEANS
    `ss 85, 86 -- how to enforce` `is it an order to pay me money`

§§ `Costs`

@export Do I bear my own costs of my Tribunal proceeding (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 87(1))? Yes, unless the Tribunal orders otherwise or the enabling Act says otherwise. A costs order can include compensation for expenses, loss, inconvenience or embarrassment (s 87(3)).
GIVEN `is there a costs order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal has made an order about the parties' costs
      `does the enabling Act say otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act says otherwise about costs
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I bear my own costs` MEANS
    `s 87(1) -- I bear my own costs` `is there a costs order` `does the enabling Act say otherwise`

@export Can the Tribunal order me to pay the costs of the proceeding itself (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 88)? In a review only if you brought or conducted it frivolously or vexatiously, did not genuinely try to help the decision-maker decide on the merits, or acted in a way that would let the Tribunal dismiss it; in its original jurisdiction it may.
GIVEN `is it a review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the matter is in the Tribunal's review jurisdiction (the answer to the review or original question)
      `was I frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you brought or conducted the proceeding frivolously or vexatiously
      `did I fail to help the decision-maker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, before the decision-maker, you failed genuinely to attempt to enable and assist them to decide on the merits
      `could it have been dismissed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether circumstances arose in which the Tribunal could dismiss or strike out under s 46 (withdrawal, want of prosecution), s 47 (frivolous, abuse) or s 48 (disadvantaging conduct)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can I be made to pay the costs of the proceeding` MEANS
    `s 88 -- I may be ordered to pay the costs of the proceeding` `is it a review` `was I frivolous or vexatious` `did I fail to help the decision-maker` `could it have been dismissed`

§§ `More time, and minor proceedings`

@export Can the Tribunal give me more time to start my case or take a step, even after the time has passed (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 92)? Where the rules provide for it, even for a time limit in the enabling Act; but never if it would cause another party prejudice that costs or damages cannot put right.
GIVEN `do the rules allow it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal's rules provide for extending this time limit (or waiving this requirement)
      `does the enabling Act expressly exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the enabling Act expressly excludes s 92
      `would it cause irreparable prejudice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether extending would cause another party or potential party prejudice or detriment that an order for costs or damages could not remedy
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the Tribunal give me more time` MEANS
    `s 92 -- the Tribunal may extend my time` `do the rules allow it` `does the enabling Act expressly exclude it` `would it cause irreparable prejudice`

@export Is my proceeding a minor proceeding, so that I can elect no lawyers, no hearing, or no appeals (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 93)? It is where a money value can be put on the matter and it is not over $10,000 ($7,500 before 1 January 2009), it is not a vocational regulatory matter and no enabling Act excludes it; or where the regulations or an enabling Act include its kind.
GIVEN `can a money value be put on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a monetary value can be ascribed to the matter in issue
      `the money value` IS A NUMBER @desc That value in dollars (0 if none)
      `the day it started` IS A DATE @desc The day the proceeding commenced
      `is it a vocational regulatory matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it deals with a decision of, or a matter brought by or under an Act of, a body controlling a person's right to pursue a vocation
      `does an enabling Act exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an enabling Act excludes this kind of proceeding from s 93
      `is its kind included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations or an enabling Act include this kind of proceeding in s 93
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my proceeding a minor proceeding` MEANS
    `s 93(1) -- it is a minor proceeding` `can a money value be put on it` `the money value` `the day it started` `is it a vocational regulatory matter` `does an enabling Act exclude it` `is its kind included`

§§ `Offences (if it has come to this)`

@export Is it an offence for me not to comply with this Tribunal decision (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 95)? Only for a decision that is not an order to pay money, and only if the Tribunal declared in the decision (or by a later order served on you, with the failure continuing) that it is; if you were not heard, only once you were given a certified copy and a copy of s 95. Maximum fine $10,000.
GIVEN `is it an order to pay money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision (or the part you are not complying with) is a monetary order
      `does it declare s 95 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tribunal declared in the decision that s 95(1) applies
      `was a later declaration served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after you failed to comply, the Tribunal ordered that s 95(1) applies, notice of the order was served on you, and the failure continued after that
      `was I heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had an opportunity to be heard before the decision was made
      `was I given the copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not: whether you were given a certified copy of the decision and a copy of s 95 (personally or as the Tribunal specified)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is not complying an offence for me` MEANS
    `s 95 -- failing to comply is an offence for me` `is it an order to pay money` `does it declare s 95 applies` `was a later declaration served` `was I heard` `was I given the copies`

@export What is the most I can be fined for an offence connected with a Tribunal proceeding (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 95-99, 103(3))? $10,000 for not complying with a declared decision, false or misleading information, or misbehaving or obstructing; $5,000 for ignoring a summons or refusing an oath or answer without reasonable excuse, or breaching a release condition.
GIVEN `which offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: failing to comply with a decision (s 95); failing to comply with a summons (s 96); refusing an oath, affirmation, declaration or answer (s 97); giving false or misleading information (s 98); misbehaving, obstructing or interrupting (s 99); breaching a condition of release after arrest (s 103(3))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be fined` MEANS
    `ss 95-99, 103 -- the maximum fine` `which offence`

§§ `Appeal`

@export Can I appeal the Tribunal's decision, and on what grounds (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) ss 44(5), 93(5), 105)? A party may appeal only with the court's leave and only on a question of law, except that a decision under a listed vocational Act that stops you lawfully pursuing your vocation can be appealed on any ground. No appeal lies from a decision on a referral of your rejected application, or after a no appeals election.
GIVEN `was I a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a party to the Tribunal proceeding
      `was it on a referral of my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was on a referral under s 44(3) or (4) about rejecting or conditionally accepting your application
      `was a no appeals election made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant in a minor proceeding made a no appeals election
      `is it a prescribed proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the proceeding is of a kind prescribed by the regulations for s 105(11)
      `have I agreed to indemnify` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you have agreed to indemnify each other party against their reasonable legal costs of the appeal
      `is it under a listed vocational Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made under (or reviewed a decision under) an Act in Schedule 1 that is the enabling Act (for example the Architects Act 2004, Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (WA), Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA), Real Estate and Business Agents Act 1978, Settlement Agents Act 1981, Teacher Registration Act 2012, Veterinary Practice Act 2021) or an Act prescribed for s 105(13)
      `does it stop me pursuing my vocation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision has the effect of depriving you of your capacity to lawfully pursue a vocation
GIVETH A MAYBE `Appeal`
`Can I appeal and on what grounds` MEANS
    `s 105 -- my appeal` `was I a party` `was it on a referral of my application` `was a no appeals election made` `is it a prescribed proceeding` `have I agreed to indemnify` `is it under a listed vocational Act` `does it stop me pursuing my vocation`

@export Which court does my appeal from the Tribunal go to (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 105(3))? The Court of Appeal if the President or a Deputy President made the decision or sat on it; otherwise the Supreme Court.
GIVEN `did a judicial member decide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was made by a judicial member (the President or a Deputy President) or by a Tribunal that included one
GIVETH AN `Appeal court`
`Which court hears my appeal` MEANS
    `s 105(3) -- the court` `did a judicial member decide`

@export By when must I apply for leave to appeal from the Tribunal's decision (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 105(5), (7))? Within 28 days after the decision is given; or, if it came without written reasons and you asked for them under s 78, within 28 days after the written reasons are given. The court may extend the time, even after it has passed.
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal gave its decision
      `did I ask for written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was given without written reasons and you then asked for them under s 78
      `have they been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether the written reasons have been given to you
      `the day they were given` IS A DATE @desc The day the written reasons were given to you (any date if not)
      `has the court extended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time
      `the extended day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if none)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I apply for leave to appeal` MEANS
    `s 105(5), (7) -- the time limit for leave` `the day of the decision` `did I ask for written reasons` `have they been given` `the day they were given` `has the court extended it` `the extended day`

@export Is my application for leave to appeal from the Tribunal in time if I make it on this day (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 105(5), (7))? The 28 days are run as a duty to apply in time; an application on the last day is in time.
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the Tribunal gave its decision
      `did I ask for written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the decision was given without written reasons and you then asked for them under s 78
      `have they been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether the written reasons have been given to you
      `the day they were given` IS A DATE @desc The day the written reasons were given to you (any date if not)
      `has the court extended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time
      `the extended day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if none)
      `the day I apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply (or would apply) for leave
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my leave application in time` MEANS
    `the person can take` `apply for leave to appeal` `running from` `the day of the decision` `under` (`By when must I apply for leave to appeal` `the day of the decision` `did I ask for written reasons` `have they been given` `the day they were given` `has the court extended it` `the extended day`) `on` `the day I apply`

@export By when must I institute my appeal once leave is granted (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 105(6), (7))? Within 21 days after the day leave is granted, unless the court extends it.
GIVEN `has leave been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has granted leave to appeal
      `the day of leave` IS A DATE @desc The day leave was granted (any date if not)
      `has the court extended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time
      `the extended day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if none)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I institute my appeal` MEANS
    `s 105(6), (7) -- the time limit to institute the appeal` `has leave been granted` `the day of leave` `has the court extended it` `the extended day`

@export Is my appeal instituted in time if I institute it on this day (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 105(6), (7))? The 21 days are run as a duty to institute in time; instituting on the last day is in time.
GIVEN `has leave been granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has granted leave to appeal
      `the day of leave` IS A DATE @desc The day leave was granted (any date if not)
      `has the court extended it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has extended the time
      `the extended day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the extended time (any date if none)
      `the day I institute` IS A DATE @desc The day you institute (or would institute) the appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my appeal instituted in time` MEANS
    `the person can take` `institute the appeal` `running from` `the day of leave` `under` (`By when must I institute my appeal` `has leave been granted` `the day of leave` `has the court extended it` `the extended day`) `on` `the day I institute`

@export Does my appeal stop the Tribunal's decision from operating (State Administrative Tribunal Act 2004 (WA) s 106)? No, unless the Supreme Court orders a stay pending the leave application and the appeal.
GIVEN `has the court ordered a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Supreme Court (or the Court of Appeal) has stayed the operation of the decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is the decision stayed by my appeal` MEANS
    `s 106 -- the decision is stayed by the appeal` `has the court ordered a stay`
